messages:
Felix: noticed a subtle but annoying issue on compact consoles: the left micro-handle (our new 6px peek stripe) overlays the table's horizontal scroller on narrow viewports causing mis-taps. Screenshot: https://redwood.app/s/ux/micro-handle-scroller.png :worried:
Nadine: which breakpoint/device? repro steps?
Felix: repro on iPhone SE & older Androids at ~340px width. We added the 6px visual stripe to reduce visual noise but the invisible hit area still uses an absolute left offset that sits on top of the scroller thumb. Users trying to pan the row hit the handle instead.
Oscar: analytics: small spike in mobile row-action cancellations in that segment last 48h. Likely same.
Tess: accessibility: overlapping interactive zones break sequential focus and make TalkBack/VoiceOver announce the handle unexpectedly. Also the handle isn't announced as focusable in some cases.
Nadine: quick mitigation ideas: (A) move the hit area so it sits under the safe-area inset (env(safe-area-inset-left)) when present; (B) switch to pointer-events:none on the visible stripe and provide a separate offscreen focusable control for keyboard/screen-reader users; (C) dynamically disable handle hit area when a .has-h-scroll container is under the pointer/touch. Pros/cons?
Carmen: love (A) + (B). We keep discoverability but avoid collision. If we hide the hit area we must ensure keyboard users can still open the rail (offscreen button in header). Also small copy tweak: change the mobile row action label from "Details" -> "View details" (more explicit).
Felix: agree on copy. Also propose a fallback: for widths <=360px convert the rail to bottom-sheet (modal) so it no longer competes with left-edge content. That way the left edge is safer for table interactions.
Tess: if we convert to bottom-sheet ensure aria-modal=true, focus trap on open, and focus returns to triggering row. Also announce "Opened details" on open.
Nadine: CSS/JS experiment I'll try:
```css
@media (max-width: 360px) {
  .peek-stripe { width: 6px; pointer-events: none; background: var(--accent); }
  .peek-hit { position: absolute; left: env(safe-area-inset-left); width: 44px; height: 44px; }
  .console-table.has-h-scroll .peek-hit{ pointer-events: none; }
}
```
```js
// detect h-scroll near pointer and temporarily disable handle
document.addEventListener('touchstart', e => {
  if (e.target.closest('.has-h-scroll')) disableHandleTemporarily()
})
```
Nadine: will prototype and push WIP PR. Also will add a small visual stroke to stripe for discoverability (per Felix).
Felix: small design note added with two variants (maintain left handle vs bottom-sheet fallback). I'll lean bottom-sheet for <=360px.
Carmen: can we ship copy-only PR for "View details" independently? It's low risk and should reduce confusion immediately.
Nadine: yes, will split: PR A copy-only, PR B for handle logic + bottom-sheet. Opening PRs now.
ux-bot: ci note - added mobile-handle-e2e test to nightly (build 2026.07.18-04).
Nadine: PRs: https://git.redwood/PR/5022 (copy-only), https://git.redwood/PR/5023 (handle+bottomsheet WIP).
Tess: after PR deploy can we run quick VoiceOver/TalkBack passes and a keyboard focus order check? I'll coordinate times.
Oscar: scheduling a 15m validation tomorrow 11am PT with Design/Frontend/A11y. Thanks everyone. :thumbsup:
